id: 30
hanzi: 为
pinyin: wéi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Preposition

meanings_summary:
  en: by (passive); as; to act as; to serve as; to become
  es: por (voz pasiva); como; hacer de; servir de; considerarse

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Preposition | Standard | used in passive constructions (often paired with 所 as 为……所……) to introduce the agent of action, or to denote serving as | empleado en construcciones pasivas (a menudo en el patrón 为……所……) para introducir el agente, o con valor de servir de | 为世人所称赞 (praised by all people in the world)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 四合院这种凝聚了东方哲学智慧的传统建筑形式，历经沧桑变迁，至今仍为中外建筑学者所赞叹。 | Sìhéyuàn zhè zhǒng níngjù le dōngfāng zhéxué zhìhuì de chuántǒng jiànzhù xíngshì, lìjīng cāngsāng biànqiān, zhìjīn réng wéi zhōngwài jiànzhù xuézhě suǒ zàntàn. | As a traditional architecture embodying Eastern philosophical wisdom, courtyards withstand shifting eras and are praised by scholars worldwide. | El siheyuan, síntesis de la sabiduría filosófica oriental, pervive tras siglos de vicisitudes y sigue siendo elogiado por arquitectos del mundo entero.
  #2 | 他不仅在学术界享有崇高威望，更被同行们一致推选为本届国际地质学会理事长。 | Tā bùjǐn zài xuéshùjiè xiǎngyǒu chónggāo wēiwàng, gèng bèi tóngháng men yīzhì tuīxuǎn wéi běnjiè guójì dìzhì xuéhuì lǐshìzhǎng. | Not only does he enjoy lofty prestige in academia, but he was also unanimously elected by peers to serve as president of the Geological Society. | No solo goza de sólido prestigio académico, sino que fue elegido por sus colegas para actuar como presidente de la Sociedad Geológica Internacional.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  为人所知 | known by people / widely recognized
  为……所吸引 | captivated by ...
  选为代表 | elected as representative
  化为乌有 | vanish into thin air / come to nothing
  变被动为主动 | turn passive into active
  转败为胜 | turn defeat into victory

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  为人师表 | wéi rén shī biǎo | serve as a paragon for others to emulate
  下不为例 | xià bù wéi lì | not to be taken as a precedent in the future
  敢作敢为 | gǎn zuò gǎn wéi | daring to act and take responsibility
  合二为一 | hé èr wéi yī | combine two into one single unit

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  为 | wéi | act; do; serve as; become; by | actuar; hacer; servir de; ser; por | 丶 | dot | hand leading an elephant by the trunk to work | 为 (wéi) | 4 | 单一结构 | Oracle bone pictograph of a human hand leading an elephant by its trunk to execute heavy physical labor. | A guiding hand leading a gentle working elephant forward to accomplish tasks (为). | Una mano humana que guía a un dócil elefante para emprender faenas pesadas (为). | 35 | IKS | 為

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A hand guiding action to serve as an agent or cause (为) marks passive agency (为……所……).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una mano guiando la acción para fungir de agente o causa (为) articula la voz pasiva (为……所……).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Versatile grammatical particle originating in Bronze script meaning 'to manage or act', central to classical passives and transformations.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Second tone: 'wéi' (35). Distinct from fourth tone preposition 'wèi' (for the sake of). Rise smoothly.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    办 | bàn | handle; manage | Eight 八 framing 力 instead of dot strokes
    力 | lì | power; strength | Single muscular stroke without inner dots
    头 | tóu | head; top | Big 大 frame with two dots on top
    买 | mǎi | buy; purchase | Hook frame 乛 over 头-like structure
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    作为 | zuòwéi | conduct; deed; as
    行为 | xíngwéi | action; behavior
    成为 | chéngwéi | become; turn into
    认为 | rènwéi | consider; deem

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 为 (wéi, second tone) functions in formal registers as a passive marker (被/为……所) or copular verb meaning 'to serve as/become'.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 为 (wéi) vs. 为 (wèi) | wèi | Second-tone 为 (wéi) denotes passivity or acting as, whereas fourth-tone 为 (wèi) marks benefactive purpose ('for the sake of').
    2 | 为 vs. 被 | bèi | 被 is the colloquial modern passive preposition, while 为……所 is an elevated literary passive structure.
    3 | 为 vs. 当 | dāng | 当 focuses on serving in a concrete professional post (当老师), while 为 covers broader functional roles (选为代表).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 中国传统四合院建筑的严整规制与深厚文化底蕴，不仅深受国人自豪珍视，更广为世界建筑界所瞩目。许多外国学者不远万里来到北京胡同，实地考察四合院的梁架雕饰，皆为其巧夺天工的匠心所折服。 | Zhōngguó chuántǒng sìhéyuàn jiànzhù de yánzhěng guīzhì yǔ shēnhòu wénhuà dǐyùn, bùjǐn shēn shòu guórén zìháo zhēnshì, gèng guǎng wéi shìjiè jiànzhùjiè suǒ zhǔmù. Xǔduō wàiguó xuézhě bùyuǎn-wànlǐ lái dào Běijīng hútòng, shídì kǎochá sìhéyuàn de liángjià diāoshì, jiē wéi qí qiǎoduó-tiāngōng de jiàngxīn suǒ zhéfú. | The rigorous structure and profound culture of Chinese courtyards are cherished domestically and noticed by the global architectural community. Foreign scholars travel to Beijing alleys, consistently captivated by the ingenious craftsmanship. | La armoniosa traza y hondo bagaje cultural del siheyuan son orgullo nacional y despiertan admiración internacional. Eruditos de todo el mundo viajan a los hutongs de Pekín, rindiéndose ante su primorosa maestría artesanal.
  #2 | 在漫长的历史长河中，优秀的中华传统美德世代相传，化为民族精神的血脉源泉。历代仁人志士以天下兴亡为己任，百折不挠，他们崇高的人格风范永远为后人所景仰与缅怀，激励着一代代青年奋发图强。 | Zài màncháng de lìshǐ chánghé zhōng, yōuxiù de Zhōnghuá chuántǒng měidé shìdài xiāngchuán, huà wéi mínzú jīngshén de xuèmài yuánquán. Lìdài rénrén-zhìshì yǐ tiānxià xīngwáng wéi jǐ rèn, bǎizhé-bùnáo, tāmen chónggāo de réngé fēngfàn yǒngyuǎn wéi hòurén suǒ jǐngyǎng yǔ miǎnhuái, jīlì zhe yīdàidài qīngnián fènfā-túqiáng. | Across Chinese history, traditional virtues passed down to become the lifeblood of national spirit. Patriots shouldered responsibility for the common good; their integrity is revered by posterity, inspiring generations to strive. | A lo largo de la historia, las virtudes clásicas se transmitieron como savia del espíritu patrio. Ilustres próceres asumieron el destino común; su entereza moral sigue siendo venerada por las generaciones venideras.
